        "summary": "The Bank of Korea sold KRW 0.45 trillion of 1-year Monetary Stabilization Bonds at a yield of 3.510%. Bids totaled KRW 0.52 trillion, compared with the planned issuance amount of KRW 0.70 trillion.",
        "published_at": "2026-11-04T10:42:02+09:00",
        "source": "Infomax"
      },
      {
        "id": "20261104164415517",
        "title": "South Korean IRS Yields Decline Across Tenors on Foreign Receiving",
        "summary": "South Korean interest rate swap yields fell across all tenors, driven by foreign bank receiving interest in longer maturities, with the 1-year IRS falling 2.00 bp to 3.5500%. Cross-currency swap SOFR rates diverged between short and long tenors.",
        "published_at": "2026-11-04T16:44:14+09:00",
        "source": "Infomax"
      },
      {
        "id": "20261104084346448",
        "title": "Korean Credit Market Draws Buying Interest in Short-Term Corporate Debt",
        "summary": "Buying interest returned to short-term corporate bonds and commercial paper after credit spreads widened in October when credit yields failed to track KTB declines. Demand was supported by end-of-year institutional fund deployments and yield pickup.",
